        "# 📦 **MODULE 1: The Scraper**\n",
        "### *YouTube Data Collection & Ingestion*\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "### 1. What it does\n",
        "This module is the **collector**. It connects to YouTube and systematically downloads the video's details (metadata) and every single comment and reply posted by viewers.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 2. Why it exists\n",
        "You cannot analyze what you don't have. This module acts as the **foundation** of the project, creating the \"ground truth\" dataset that all other AI modules will analyze later.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 3. How it works\n",
        "It takes a YouTube link, logs into Google's servers, and asks for data page-by-page. It keeps asking until it has every comment, then it cleans the data (removing the owner's own comments) and saves it to a file.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 4. Algorithms Involved\n",
        "*   **Exponential Backoff:** A \"smart wait\" algorithm. If YouTube's server is busy or crashes, this pauses the script for longer and longer periods to prevent errors.\n",
        "*   **Owner Filtering:** A logic check that identifies the video creator and removes their comments from the dataset so the analysis remains unbiased.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 5. Final Output\n",
        "*   **`metadata_{id}.json`**: A small file containing video stats (Views, Likes, Channel Name).\n",
        "*   **`comments_{id}.parquet`**: A high-speed data file containing the clean, structured list of thousands of comments.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "### ⚙️ **The Pipeline Logic (Step-by-Step)**\n",
        "\n",
        "This is the simple data flow of the code:\n",
        "\n",
        "**Step 1: 🆔 Get the ID**\n",
        "> **Function:** `extract_video_id`\n",
        "> The code looks at the link you pasted (e.g., `youtube.com/watch?v=XYZ`) and pulls out the unique ID (`XYZ`). If the link is bad, it stops.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Step 2: 📊 Get Video Stats**\n",
        "> **Function:** `get_video_metadata`\n",
        "> It asks YouTube for the \"Big Picture\": How many views? Who posted this?\n",
        "> *   **Crucial Step:** It memorizes the **Channel ID** of the owner so it can recognize them later.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Step 3: 📥 Download Comments**\n",
        "> **Function:** `get_all_comments`\n",
        "> It starts a loop, grabbing 100 comments at a time. It grabs the comment text, the author's name, and how many likes it got. It keeps looping until it hits the end.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Step 4: 🧹 Clean & Save**\n",
        "> **Function:** `execute_module_1`\n",
        "> This is the \"Manager\" function that runs the whole show.\n",
        "> 1.  It runs Steps 1, 2, and 3.\n",
        "> 2.  **Filter:** It compares every comment author against the Owner ID from Step 2. If they match, it deletes that comment.\n",
        "> 3.  **Save:** It saves the final clean list into a **Parquet file**, ready for the next module."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "n6HmAF5l3g1o"
      }
    },
