        "# 📦 **MODULE 2: The Analyzer**\n",
        "### *Spark Analytics & Topic Modeling*\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "### 1. What it does\n",
        "This module serves as the **Data Processing & Pattern Recognition engine**. It uses **PySpark** (a Big Data tool) to clean the raw comments and automatically figure out what people are talking about (Topics) without human help.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 2. Why it exists\n",
        "Raw text from Module 1 is \"messy\" (full of emojis, weird symbols, and junk words). This module scrubs the data clean and transforms text into numbers so the machine can understand it. It prepares the data for the final AI predictions.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 3. How it works\n",
        "It loads the Parquet file from Module 1. It detects the language (English or Arabic) and applies specific cleaning rules. Then, it runs a **Machine Learning Pipeline** to group similar comments together into \"Topics\" (e.g., \"Video Quality,\" \"Content,\" \"Spam\") and saves the results.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 4. Algorithms Involved\n",
        "*   **StopWords Removal:** A filter that deletes useless words (like \"the,\" \"is,\" \"video,\" \"reply\") so the AI focuses only on meaningful keywords.\n",
        "*   **TF/CountVectorizer:** An algorithm that counts how often words appear, turning text into numerical vectors.\n",
        "*   **LDA (Latent Dirichlet Allocation):** An unsupervised learning algorithm that looks at all comments and finds hidden \"Topics\" based on words that appear together frequently.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 5. Final Output\n",
        "*   **`topics_{id}.json`**: A list of the Top 3 detected topics and their keywords (e.g., Topic 1: [\"game\", \"play\", \"cool\"]).\n",
        "*   **`comments_ready_for_ml.parquet`**: The fully processed dataset with a new column `clean_text_ml`, ready for Module 3.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "### ⚙️ **The Pipeline Logic (Step-by-Step)**\n",
        "\n",
        "This is the flow of the code:\n",
        "\n",
        "**Step 1: ⚡ Fire Up Spark**\n",
        "> **Function:** `SparkSession.builder...`\n",
        "> It starts a local Big Data engine. It allocates memory (4GB) to handle heavy data processing tasks that normal Python might struggle with.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Step 2: 🧹 Smart Cleaning (The Factory)**\n",
        "> **Function:** `clean_text_factory`\n",
        "> It checks if the video is **Arabic** or **English**.\n",
        "> *   **If Arabic:** It removes diacritics (Tashkeel) and normalizes letters (like converting 'أ' to 'ا').\n",
        "> *   **If English:** It removes special characters and lowercases everything.\n",
        "> *   It then applies this cleaning to every single comment in parallel.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Step 3: 🧠 The Topic Machine (ML Pipeline)**\n",
        "> **Logic:** `Pipeline(Tokenizer -> Remover -> Vectorizer -> LDA)`\n",
        "> If there are enough comments (>5), it creates a pipeline:\n",
        "> 1.  **Split:** Breaks sentences into words.\n",
        "> 2.  **Filter:** Removes \"junk\" words defined in `get_stopwords`.\n",
        "> 3.  **Vectorize:** Turns words into math.\n",
        "> 4.  **Cluster:** The **LDA model** groups comments into 3 distinct topics.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Step 4: 🏷️ Tag & Save**\n",
        "> **Logic:** `model.transform`\n",
        "> It looks at every comment and assigns it a \"Dominant Topic\" ID (0, 1, or 2). Finally, it saves the clean data and the topic list to the disk.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "Here are the specific **Spark methods** used in Module 2 and what they do:\n",
        "\n",
        "### ⚡ **Setup & Loading**\n",
        "*   **`SparkSession.builder`**: Starts the \"engine.\" It configures how much memory (RAM) to use and prepares Spark to run on your computer.\n",
        "*   **`read.parquet`**: The \"fast loader.\" It reads the compressed data file from Module 1 instantly, much faster than standard file reading.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 🛠️ **Data Transformation (The DataFrame API)**\n",
        "*   **`F.udf` (User Defined Function)**: The \"converter.\" It takes your custom Python cleaning code and wraps it so Spark can run it on thousands of rows at once.\n",
        "*   **`withColumn`**: The \"adder.\" It creates a new column in your data table (e.g., adding the cleaned text next to the raw text).\n",
        "*   **`filter`**: The \"gatekeeper.\" It removes useless data, like empty rows or comments that are too short to analyze.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 🧠 **Machine Learning Tools (MLlib)**\n",
        "*   **`RegexTokenizer`**: The \"splitter.\" It chops sentences into individual words (tokens) using spaces as the cutting point.\n",
        "*   **`StopWordsRemover`**: The \"cleaner.\" It takes the list of words and deletes \"junk\" words (like \"the\", \"video\", \"is\") so only meaningful keywords remain.\n",
        "*   **`CountVectorizer`**: The \"counter.\" It converts words into numbers. It counts how many times each word appears so the computer can do math on them.\n",
        "*   **`Pipeline`**: The \"chain.\" It glues the Splitter, Cleaner, and Counter together so they run automatically in one smooth sequence.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 🤖 **The Model (AI)**\n",
        "*   **`LDA`**: The \"pattern finder.\" It scans the numeric data to find groups of words that appear together (clustering them into Topics).\n",
        "*   **`fit`**: The \"learner.\" It runs the data through the Pipeline and LDA to learn the patterns.\n",
        "*   **`transform`**: The \"predictor.\" It takes what it learned and tags each comment with the Topic it belongs to.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 💾 **Saving**\n",
        "*   **`write.parquet`**: The \"saver.\" It saves the processed data to a new file, optimized for the next module."
      ],
