        "# 📦 **MODULE 3: The AI Brain**\n",
        "### *Inference, Classification & Smart Replies*\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "### 1. What it does\n",
        "This module is the **Intelligence Layer**. It takes the cleaned text from Module 2 and passes it through **5 different AI models**. It figures out how the viewer feels, what they want, and even writes a draft reply for you.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 2. Why it exists\n",
        "Reading thousands of comments is impossible. This module automates the understanding process. It separates \"Signal\" (genuine questions, praise) from \"Noise\" (spam, hate) and automates engagement by drafting responses.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 3. How it works\n",
        "It loads specialized \"Pre-trained Transformers\" (Mini-Brains) from HuggingFace. It processes comments in batches to determine:\n",
        "1.  Is it positive or negative?\n",
        "2.  What specific emotion is shown?\n",
        "3.  Is it spam?\n",
        "4.  Is it a question?\n",
        "5.  **Smart Agent:** If the comment is good, it uses a text-generator model to write a reply.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 4. Models Involved (The Model Registry)\n",
        "*   **DistilBERT (Sentiment):** Determines if a comment is Positive, Negative, or Neutral.\n",
        "*   **RoBERTa (Emotion):** Detects specific feelings (Joy, Anger, Sadness, Surprise).\n",
        "*   **TinyBERT (Spam):** A tiny, fast model that flags junk comments.\n",
        "*   **Mini-BERT (Question):** Detects if the user is asking a question vs. making a statement.\n",
        "*   **Flan-T5 (Generator):** A \"Text-to-Text\" model (like a mini-GPT) that writes the actual replies.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 5. Final Output\n",
        "*   **`comments_classified.parquet`**: The \"Super DataFrame.\" It contains the original text plus new AI columns:\n",
        "    *   `sentiment`: \"Positive\"\n",
        "    *   `emotion`: \"Joy\"\n",
        "    *   `is_spam`: False\n",
        "    *   `is_question`: True\n",
        "    *   `suggested_reply`: \"Thank you! We used Python for the backend.\"\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "### ⚙️ **The Pipeline Logic (Step-by-Step)**\n",
        "\n",
        "This is the flow of the code:\n",
        "\n",
        "**Step 1: 🧠 Load the Brains**\n",
        "> **Function:** `get_pipeline`\n",
        "> The code downloads/loads the 4 classification models. It uses \"Distilled\" (smaller) versions of models so they run fast on a standard computer without needing a supercomputer GPU.\n",
