        "# 📦 **MODULE 4: The Teacher**\n",
        "### *Model Fine-Tuning & Domain Adaptation*\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "### 1. What it does\n",
        "This module is the **Training Center**. It takes the data labeled by Module 3 and uses it to teach a **new, specialized AI model**. Instead of relying on generic models, it creates a \"custom expert\" tailored specifically for YouTube data.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 2. Why it exists\n",
        "Generic models (Module 3) are \"Jacks of all trades.\" This module creates a \"Master of One.\" By training on the actual comments, this new model becomes smaller, faster, and more accurate at understanding specific YouTube slang, questions, and spam patterns.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 3. How it works\n",
        "It acts like a school.\n",
        "1.  **Study Material:** It loads the classified comments from Module 3.\n",
        "2.  **The Student:** It downloads a base model (`DistilBERT`).\n",
        "3.  **The Lesson:** It forces the model to read thousands of comments and predict tags (Spam, Question, Supportive).\n",
        "4.  **Grading:** It checks the answers, corrects the model, and repeats the process (Epochs) until the model gets a high score.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 4. Algorithms Involved\n",
        "*   **DistilBERT (Multilingual):** The base \"brain\" being taught. It understands many languages but needs fine-tuning for this specific task.\n",
        "*   **AdamW Optimizer:** The algorithm that adjusts the model's \"neurons\" to minimize errors during training.\n",
        "*   **Binary Cross Entropy:** The math used to calculate how \"wrong\" a guess was for multi-label tasks (e.g., a comment can be BOTH a \"Question\" AND \"Supportive\").\n",
        "\n",
        "### 5. Final Output\n",
        "*   **`saved_models/yt_insight_finetuned_v1/`**: A folder containing the trained \"Brain.\"\n",
        "    *   `pytorch_model.bin`: The actual learned weights.\n",
        "    *   `tokenizer.json`: The dictionary it uses to understand words.\n",
        "    *   **Result:** A portable AI model you can use anywhere without internet.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "### ⚙️ **The Pipeline Logic (Step-by-Step)**\n",
        "\n",
        "This is the flow of the  code:\n",
        "\n",
        "**Step 1: 📝 Data Prep (The Textbook)**\n",
        "> **Function:** `pd.read_parquet` & `Dataset Class`\n",
        "> It loads the data and ensures the \"Target Columns\" exist:\n",
        "> *   `is_question` (Did they ask something?)\n",
        "> *   `is_spam` (Is it junk?)\n",
        "> *   `is_supportive` (Are they being nice?)\n",
