        "\n",
        "### 🔗 The Final Connection Map\n",
        "Here is the definitive guide to how code turns **Raw Data** into **Strategy**.\n",
        "\n",
        "| Strategy Section | Powered By Which Model? | How it works (The Logic) |\n",
        "| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n",
        "| **1. The Vibe Check** | **DistilBERT** (Sentiment) + **RoBERTa** (Emotion) | It compares the count of `positive` labels vs `negative` labels to give a \"Mood Score\". |\n",
        "| **2. Burning Questions** | **MiniBERT** (Question Classifier) | It uses a specialized AI model trained to recognize inquisitive sentences (Who/What/Where) to filter the list. |\n",
        "| **3. The 'Money' Topic** | **Spark LDA** (Module 2) | It calculates which **Topic Group** (from Spark) has the highest average **Like Count** to identify what viewers value most. |\n",
        "| **4. Superfan Spotlight** | **Scraper** (Module 1) | It simply counts which `author_id` appears most frequently in the dataset (excluding the owner). |\n",
        "| **5. Moderation Radar** | **TinyBERT** (Spam Classifier) | It uses a lightweight AI model trained on SMS spam to flag comments that look like ads or scams. |\n",
        "| **6. SEO Keywords** | **Spark Cleaning** (Module 2) | It looks at the `clean_text_ml` column (stopwords removed) and finds the most frequent words. |\n",
        "| **7. Timing Optimization** | **Scraper** (Module 1) | It extracts the hour (0-23) from the `published_at` timestamp and finds the most common hour. |\n",
        "| **8. Controversy Meter** | **RoBERTa** (Emotion) | It specifically looks for the **\"anger\"** label from the Emotion model. High anger = High controversy. |\n",
        "| **9. Quick Reply Ops** | **Flan-T5** (Generative AI) | It reads the user's comment and \"writes\" a brand new, context-aware response using a Seq2Seq model. |\n",
        "| **10. Next Video Idea** | **Spark LDA** (Module 2) | It takes the top words from the most popular Topic and inserts them into a YouTube title template (e.g., \"X Explained\"). |\n",
        "\n"
      ]
    }
